# Arena Liferay Portal 7.0.6-ga7-specific Aikido scan excludes.
# One pattern per line (# comments allowed), passed as --exclude to the
# aikido-scan wrapper.
# Kept here (repo root) rather than in the aikido-scan skill so the skill
# itself stays portable to other projects unmodified.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCLUDE SEMANTICS - measured against local-scanner v1.0.139 on 2026-08-29
# (synthetic-repo probe; see KnowledgeBase docs/security/aikido-security-scanning.md).
# `--exclude` is a plain, CASE-SENSITIVE SUBSTRING match on the candidate
# path. It is NOT a glob and NOT a path matcher:
#   * any pattern containing `*` is INERT and fails silently: `docs/**`,
#     `**/src/test/**` and `modules/**/bin/**` match nothing at all.
#   * a bare word matches anywhere inside a path, mid-name included:
#     `build` also excludes `service-builder/` and every `build.gradle`;
#     `bin` also excludes `binding`, `binary`, `combine`; `sql` also
#     excludes `mysql`/`postgresql`. Silent over-exclusion, and excluding
#     build.gradle blinds dependency scanning entirely.
#   * the correct idiom is a SLASH-WRAPPED segment: `/build/` matches every
#     directory named exactly `build`, at any depth, and nothing else.
#   * there is NO root anchoring. `/bin/` hits nested bin dirs as well as the
#     top-level one; the pre-2026-08-29 claim that a slash makes a pattern
#     "start-anchored and immune to minimatch matchBase" was wrong on both
#     counts - minimatch is not what does the matching.
#   * the secrets stage (gitleaks) ignores --exclude entirely and walks
#     everything; only pre-scan cleanup or --scan-types affects its cost.
# The scan wrapper warns about inert patterns before every scan.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# IDE-generated build/compiled-class output for the Ant-built core modules
# (portal-impl, portal-kernel, portal-test, portal-test-integration,
# support-tomcat, util-bridges, util-java, util-slf4j, util-taglib, ...).
# This repo's own .gitignore predates these paths (it lists per-module
# classes/test-classes/woven-classes, not build/) so they show up untracked.
# Verified via `git ls-files | grep -E "(^|/)build/"` - zero tracked files
# live under any build/ directory anywhere in this repo, so this is safe.
/build/

# Stray JVM heap dump left in the working tree (modules/apps/foundation/
# portal/java_pid83209.hprof) - not build output, but pure scan noise either
# way. Consider deleting it directly; it may contain sensitive memory
# contents and has no reason to exist in the working tree.
.hprof

# NOTE: node_modules is intentionally NOT excluded here. Aikido's JS
# supply-chain coverage (package-lock.json / node_modules CVEs) is real
# scanning surface, not noise - unlike the palma-style scope exclusions
# elsewhere, this is a security-coverage decision, not cleanup. If scan
# time/volume becomes a problem, discuss before adding an exclude for it.
# NOTE: "scripts" and "readme" are deliberately NOT in this list. scripts/
# holds this branch's own security tooling (sweep-deps.sh,
# deploy-maven-artifacts.sh); excluding it would silently hide that from
# scanning.
#
# NOTE (2026-08-29): these were bare words and were over-matching badly.
# Bare `gradle` dropped 1160 tracked files that are not in a gradle/ dir -
# every build.gradle / settings.gradle / gradle.properties in the repo -
# which silently disabled Gradle dependency scanning. Bare `sql` dropped 69
# (mysql/postgresql/sqlserver names), `bin` 16 (binding/binary/...) and
# `definitions` 15. The slash-wrapped forms below match only directories
# with those exact names, so the scan now covers more than it did.
/bin/
/benchmarks/
/classes/
/definitions/
/gradle/
/sql/
/support-resin/
/support-websphere/

# opensocial-portlet: confirmed never deployed through arena-parent (its
# .war is excluded from the published com.liferay.portal.osgi zip in
# scripts/deploy-maven-artifacts.sh) - exclude the whole module rather than
# tracking its vendored blobs (OpenAjax_Hub_2.0.5_r1293.zip,
# shindig-server-2.0.2.war, ...) one file at a time as new ones surface.
/modules/apps/opensocial/opensocial-portlet/

# Single vendored source archive (the path form works as a plain substring).
modules/apps/wiki-engine-mediawiki/wiki-engine-mediawiki/jamwiki-1.0.7-src.zip
